PART 1 -- the action grammar, read from the engine and measured.
====================================================================================================
valid_actions, read from rmgpy/data/kinetics/family.py:
  ['CHANGE_BOND', 'FORM_BOND', 'BREAK_BOND', 'GAIN_RADICAL', 'LOSE_RADICAL', 'GAIN_CHARGE', 'LOSE_CHARGE', 'GAIN_PAIR', 'LOSE_PAIR']

Effect of each on the DERIVED charge of *1, measured by applying it and reading back:

  action              labels  d(charge)  meaning
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  GAIN_RADICAL             1         -1  moves +1 electron(s) onto *1
  LOSE_RADICAL             1         +1  moves -1 electron(s) onto *1
  GAIN_PAIR                1         -2  moves +2 electron(s) onto *1
  LOSE_PAIR                1         +2  moves -2 electron(s) onto *1
  GAIN_CHARGE              1         +0  moves NO electron
  LOSE_CHARGE              1         +0  moves NO electron
  CHANGE_BOND(+1)          2         -1  moves +1 electron(s) onto *1
  BREAK_BOND               2         +1  moves -1 electron(s) onto *1
  FORM_BOND                2         -1  moves +1 electron(s) onto *1

Reading: an electron arriving at an atom must lower valence - bonds - radicals - 2*lp by
one. GAIN_RADICAL does exactly that with one label. GAIN_PAIR/LOSE_PAIR move two
electrons. Bond actions move one onto EACH of two atoms and need a second label. The two
charge actions move none -- they are the only actions in the grammar with no effect on
the quantity the charge is derived from.

